1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.957
Compare decimal amounts

2
00:00:01.957 --> 00:00:31.957
Namaste! Aaj ka lesson hai Compare decimal amounts. Decimal numbers compare karte waqt place value aur equal decimal places dekho. Is baat ko dheere-dheere samjhenge, phir ek aasaan example dekhenge. Learning mein galti hona bilkul normal hai; hum har step ko dobara check kar sakte hain.

3
00:00:31.957 --> 00:01:04.565
₹5.40, ₹5.04 se zyada hai kyunki 40 paise, 4 paise se zyada hain. Dhyaan do ki example mein kaunsi cheez badal rahi hai aur kaunsi same rehti hai. Pehle apna andaaza bolo, phir reason dhoondo. Agar tum kisi dost ko samjha sakte ho, to concept aur mazboot ho jaata hai.

4
00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:41.087
Dono numbers ke tenths aur hundredths ko alag rang se underline karke compare karo. Apne observation ko ek sentence mein likho. Har number ya label ke saath sahi unit ya naam lagao. Sawaal solve karte waqt jaldi mat karo; clue ko underline karo, apna tareeka chuno, aur aakhir mein jawab ko example ke saath compare karo.

5
00:01:41.087 --> 00:02:57.391
Ab practice karo: Kaunsa bada hai: 3.60 ya 3.06? Thoda rukkar socho. Sahi jawab hai 3.60. Baaki options kyun fit nahi hote, yeh bhi apne shabdon mein batao. Decimal numbers compare karte waqt place value aur equal decimal places dekho. ₹5.40, ₹5.04 se zyada hai kyunki 40 paise, 4 paise se zyada hain. Is idea ko yaad rakhne ke liye apni notebook mein ek chhota labelled drawing banao. Jab tum apne shabdon mein samjha paate ho, tab tumne sirf answer nahi yaad kiya, balki uska reason bhi samjha. Aaj ka chhota recap: Decimal numbers compare karte waqt place value aur equal decimal places dekho. Agli baar aas-paas ki duniya mein isi idea ka ek aur example dhoondhna.

